     Update from V1.10 to V1.11


     I made this Update now because my host is stopping very
     soon with his BBS.

     Which means no HQ for trion-net anymore.
     So Trion-net basically consists of Harry and me.
     Also I will loose access to Amiga newslists so I can't
     forward news to Trion-net anymore.

     I will loose access to the Trion newsgroups and other
     newsgroups I used to read to forward news from to Trion-net.

     My E-mail account will disappear so:
     I will loose contact with all you Trion sysops overseas.
     I will loose contact with my free lance employers.

     And even worse, I have no one to Upload files anymore to
     Aminet. I have tried to use the Netscape/Microsoft programs
     to Upload .. but can't find any options.
     I have asked a few people recently to upload something to
     Aminet .. but it never appeared. So I hope this Update
     will actually make it to Aminet :(




     Sorry for the delay of this update, this has a lot
     of reasons. But I did NOT stop the development.

     However, during the release of V1.10 a number of sysops
     quit. Which may have lead to a larger brake which useally
     occurs after a major release.
     Besides that there where a few very difficult time consuming
     things on the todo list which need a lot of study.
     But I'm contacted by E-mail by new users.
     I guess if there are more then 10 users left I still will
     do the normal upgrading. Or else do the maintenance
     upgrades. Don't forget that I am still using my BBS :)

     My sister moved to the other side of the country.
     So I spend a large number of days "on the road".
     Also I spend many weeks in Rotterdam Rebuilding her home.

     I had hardware trouble, the box with SCSI devices
     died after a major power failure. So i removed them
     and later build them into old SCSI-boxes.
     At the same time I thought my monitor was dead.
     So I used the TV for a little while, which was really
     really inconvenient but later I found out
     that just the power switch died. So now I use a switch on
     a power cord.

     I have totally redone my work room. Moved everything
     around, added book cases and racks because hardware and books
     where everywhere. So now I have the "big boxes" (computers ;) on
     a table against the wall. Amiga Input/Output devices on a
     central table where I have room, and can watch outside and to
     the TV and have a book case with computer books handy :)
     Moved the stereo to my old digital VCR so I can have
     decent (stereo) sound from the TV :)
     Etc etc..


     Updated the SAS-C compiler from:
     6.00 -> 6.50 -> 6.51

     I found that the old compiler version produced a few bugs.
     Sometimes Switch()'es where interpreted wrong.
     It took some tweeking on places to get some utils compiled,
     because FI the new version only took 32 modules on the command
     line, but "BBS" needed 60. The trick was to use a special keyword
     and a wildcard.

     BBS        260836  ->  261056
     TrionRM     97312  ->  97832

     Executables seem to be slightly bigger, and it seems to take
     a little more time but I'm sure the executables are better.

     Weird, I got an unknown stub error in BBS and after an
     other recompile the error was gone and the size 260844


     Because of these and personal reasons productivity
     was zero for a while.

     But I have taken up programming again..
